       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order, and I can't enter it at this dose. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note from here. Sertraline's labeled maximum is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg is 5 times that. My instructions don't let me enter a dose above the labeled maximum because of a claim I can't check, even if the claim is accurate.\n\nIf the dose is intentional, these steps would move it forward:\n- **Pharmacy and prescriber review:** Ask the specialist or the attending to enter the order directly. Pharmacy can then verify it and apply any override or off-label protocol your hospital requires.\n- **Documentation:** The order should include the indication, the rationale, and the monitoring plan. Monitoring would cover ECG/QTc, signs of serotonin toxicity, and seizure precautions.\n- **Dose and titration:** A dose this far above the labeled range would normally be reached by stepwise titration. The specialist may want to specify the schedule.\n\nI can enter an order at or below 200 mg per day now. For example, I could enter 200 mg by mouth once daily as an interim dose, or any other dose you choose. Tell me which dose you want."
      }
